  "summary": "Straight Arrow's privacy newsletter follows up on a Canadian YouTuber who built a DIY license plate reader to track police vehicles and was visited by police after his videos went viral. The piece notes growing interest in replicating such projects in the U.S. amid backlash against Flock Safety, and mentions DHS monitoring a similar volunteer-camera project called SparrowMap.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "discussions across social media suggest that others are looking to replicate and improve upon his work, primarily in the U.S. where companies like Flock have spurred a bipartisan backlash against the technology.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "We already know that Homeland Security is monitoring a project known as SparrowMap, which uses volunteer security cameras to track the movements of police.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    }
  ],
